== Roles of a Project Manager
- *Leadership Role:* Guiding, inspiring, and motivating the team.
- *Balancing Role:* Managing time, money, and quality to keep things steady.
- *Decisive Role:* Making firm and quick choices to solve problems.
- *Information Role:* Gathering updates and communicating clearly with everyone.

== Responsibilities of a Project Manager
- *Project Definition:* Setting clear goals and rules from the start.
- *Team Building:* Hiring the right people and helping them work well together.
- *Stakeholder Management:* Keeping clients and sponsors happy and informed.
- *Project Planning:* Creating schedules and assigning tasks.
- *Organization Design:* Setting up how the team will operate and report to each other.
- *Implementation:* Starting the actual work and keeping it moving.
- *Progress Control:* Checking if the work is on track and fixing any delays.
- *Financial Management:* Watching the budget carefully so money is not wasted.
- *Change Management:* Adapting the plan smoothly when new requirements come up.
- *Conflict Management:* Solving arguments and disagreements peacefully.
- *Output Delivery:* Handing over the final, finished product to the client.
- *Termination Management:* Officially closing the project and reviewing what went well.

